<p>Image Sources:<a href="https://static.pexels.com/photos/169972/pexels-photo-169972.jpeg">https://static.pexels.com/photos/169972/pexels-photo-169972.jpeg</a><br />
<a href="https://static.pexels.com/photos/7695/night-white-black-contrast.jpg">https://static.pexels.com/photos/7695/night-white-black-contrast.jpg</a><br />
<a href="https://static.pexels.com/photos/15271/pexels-photo-15271.jpg">https://static.pexels.com/photos/15271/pexels-photo-15271.jpg</a></p>
<p>This SCP is technically a collaboration since the idea for the Matinee was originally that of <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/peppersghost" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1553042); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1553042&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1515552272" alt="PeppersGhost" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1553042)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/peppersghost" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1553042); return false;">PeppersGhost</a></span>, which he shared with me in an email. I fleshed it out and incorporated it into the Dread &amp; Circuses continuity.</p>
<p><strong>Edit:</strong> As some of you may be aware, PeppersGhost (creator of Herman Fuller) is not currently an active member of the site. As such my communication with him is very intermittent, and because I really wanted this up for October I posted it without his approval. I should not have done that and I apologize.</p>
<p>Fortunately, Pepper is very reasonable and is willing to let this remain up, but has requested that I acknowledge I acted without his permission. There exists the possibility that he may significantly alter this article or replace it entirely in the future, as is his right.</p>
<p>Thanks to all the beta readers who read this and/or its companion tale:</p>
