			<div class="content" id="post-content-3612908">
									

<p>I really like the idea of Herman having a theater where people are used as marionettes for being disobedient. It further added to the cruelty of the circus. Though I do have issues with this that lead to my down vote.</p>
<p>It doesn't stand on its own since it requires a bit of context to understand and I believe that SCP articles are to be done first and separate and then be incorporated into canon series instead of being made for a canon so readers can have more foundation for their own head canons. Here it is already established and the narrative is hard to ignore and the only canon that makes sense for one to make is what was provided to them being the tale which sorta leads to my next point.</p>
<p>Herman Fuller is in the article. I feel it's better that Herman is just this mysterious dude we hardly see but just know he is a cruel and cunning guy who feels little to no emotions towards others in the circus. It be better if this article was written if Fuller was still in charge instead of part of the canon it was made for. To have him just suddenly be in an article makes him feel not so special, especially him just defeated. It feels better for such characters to be explored heavily in tales rather than main list SCPs.</p>

							</div>

								
					
