<p>That's kind of weird a question. It wouldn't work without its anomalous components, I can say that at least. It basically records a person's aether waves (magic) with an aetherscope (magic), plays them on a thaumaphone (magic) by sending the waves through thaumically conducting wires (magic) into corpses that still have their souls in them (magic), and the machine itself is protected by an indestructible copper patina (magic) and its internal workings are based on Broken Mechatronics (magic). That's at least seven separate magic components, so it's pretty magical.</p>
